course: dictionary
lesson: 13762
title: Interpret: explaining what something means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To interpret something is to explain or decide what it means. You can interpret a poem, a graph or a look on a friend's face. «The teacher asked us to interpret the poem about the storm.» We read it closely, think about the words, and say what it means.
explain: Interpret can also mean to translate aloud what someone says as they speak. «Mrs Okafor is an interpreter, so she turned the doctor's words into Polish for the family.» She listened and spoke the new language at the same time.
explain: You can also interpret music, a role in a play or a dance by performing it in your own way. Two actors can interpret the same character differently, and both can be right. Context helps here too: look at the words around an unknown word and ask what would fit.
fact: Interpret is a verb: interpret, interprets, interpreted, interpreting.
fact: «Interpret» means to explain or decide what something means.
fact: In maths and science, you interpret a graph when you say what the numbers show.
fact: An interpreter helps people who speak different languages, or uses sign language, by translating as they talk.
fact: When you interpret a poem, you give your own meaning, but it should match the words of the poem.
exercise: «The graph shows that sales went up in June.» What does it mean to interpret this graph? | *To say what the numbers show | To count the pages | To colour it in with paint | To throw it away
exercise: «Mrs Okafor is an interpreter at the hospital.» What does an interpreter do? | *Helps people who speak different languages by translating as they speak | Cooks food for the patients | Drives the ambulance | Cleans the floors
exercise: Ella says, «Yesterday we interpreted a poem about the sea.» Which word is the past form of interpret? | interpreter | *interpreted | interpreting | interprets
test: Ella wants to interpret a poem about the sea. What is she doing? | Measuring the waves | Swimming in the sea | *Explaining what the poem means | Painting the sand
test: «The dancer interpreted the sad song with slow, soft movements.» What does interpreted mean here? | *Performed it in her own way | Sang it backwards | Wrote a new song about it | Forgot the song
exam: Which sentence uses interpret to mean translate aloud as someone speaks? | «He interpreted the cake in the oven.» | «The children interpreted their bedroom at bedtime.» | *«She interpreted the French speaker's words into English as he talked.» | «The bridge interpreted the river for the boats.»
